    <string name="app_name">App-Block</string>
    <string name="accessibility_label">App-Block detection</string>
    <string name="accessibility_description">Detects which apps are on screen (including split-screen panes) so App-Block can show the block screen when a budgeted app is visible. Reads which app owns each window, the text of system Settings screens so it can guard its own toggle, and — in your chosen web browsers — the address bar, so blocked websites can be caught. It does not read page content or other apps.</string>
    <string name="block_title">Blocked</string>
    <string name="block_message">You chose to block this app. Take a breath and go back.</string>
    <string name="block_message_bypass_tool">This app can hand adb-level control to other apps, which is enough to switch App-Block off. It is blocked permanently and can\'t be unblocked from the phone.</string>
    <string name="block_message_budget">You\'ve used up today\'s time for %1$s. It resets at 4am.</string>
    <string name="block_message_schedule">%1$s is outside its allowed hours right now. It opens again in its next window.</string>
    <string name="block_message_tamper">Clock tampering detected. Everything stays blocked until BOTH automatic date &amp; time AND automatic time zone are back on in Settings.</string>
    <string name="block_message_site">This site is on your blocklist. Removing it takes the 72-hour change window.</string>
    <string name="block_message_site_named">%1$s is on your blocklist. Removing it takes the 72-hour change window.</string>
    <string name="block_message_browser">This browser isn\'t on your allowed list. Use Chrome or Brave.</string>
    <string name="block_message_web_app">This is a website installed as an app, so it has no address bar to check against your blocklist. Open the site in Chrome instead.</string>
    <string name="block_message_unreadable">App-Block can\'t read this browser\'s address bar, so it can\'t tell which site you\'re on. Blocked until it can — if this keeps happening, the browser has probably updated.</string>
    <string name="block_go_back">Go back</string>
    <!--
      The block screen's two fact rows, filled in per block from com.appblock.engine.BlockFacts.

      REPLACED 2026-08-05 (was: block_fact_resets/_value + block_fact_more_time/_value, four fixed
      strings baked into overlay_block.xml). They read "day resets 04:00" and "more time 1-hour wait"
      under EVERY block, which is true of a budget block and false of the other five. The two that
      matter: a schedule block is not waiting on 04:00 and cannot be shortened by any wait at all
      (PolicyEngine.scheduleAllows gates before the budget path, so an exception raises a cap that
      isn't what stopped you), and a blocked site costs the 72-hour cycle, not an hour.

      Labels — the left column, one per Returns/Route case.
    -->
