    <string name="lock_export">Keep a copy of your rules</string>
    <string name="lock_export_body">Copies your caps, schedules, blocked apps and blocked sites as plain text. If this phone is ever wiped, that text is the only record — App-Block can\'t read it back in, so you\'d re-enter it by hand. Your lock key is never included.</string>
    <string name="lock_export_copy">Copy rules</string>
    <string name="lock_export_done">Rules copied. Paste them somewhere that survives this phone.</string>
    <string name="protection_rules_unreadable">Your saved rules couldn\'t be read</string>
    <string name="protection_rules_unreadable_body">App-Block fell back to its built-in defaults, so any app you added yourself is no longer blocked. Rebuild what\'s missing in Apps — adding and tightening are always free. The unreadable copy has been kept.</string>
    <string name="protection_reels_stale">Reels detection needs a re-check</string>
    <string name="protection_reels_stale_body">Instagram has updated since App-Block last recognised the Reels player. Open Reels once — if you get the block screen it still works and this disappears. If you don\'t, the Reels rule has stopped working.</string>
    <!--
      The in-app half of the omnibox-drift canary, deferred 2026-08-03 and added 2026-08-05.

      Deliberately states BOTH directions, because the two drift canaries fail opposite ways and this
      one changes direction at exactly the moment the row appears. Reels drift only ever under-blocks.
      Address-bar drift under-blocks for the seven days OmniboxWitnessStore vouches through, then
      over-blocks once AddressWatch withdraws the vouch and an unreadable bar counts as Unreadable.
      One sentence for each, and the same re-check clears both.
    -->
    <string name="protection_omnibox_stale">Website blocking needs a re-check</string>
    <string name="protection_omnibox_stale_body">Your browser updated a week ago and App-Block hasn\'t managed to read its address bar since, so it can\'t tell which site you\'re on. Until it can, blocked sites may have been slipping through — and from now on pages it can\'t read get blocked instead. Open the browser on any page with the address bar showing: that re-checks it and clears this either way.</string>
    <string name="action_grant">Grant</string>
    <string name="action_enable">Enable</string>
